checked_ok:
No generator drops a case:
- mix: n challenge theorems plus n² branch theorems plus Passes per family, which covers every conjunct of mixAcceptsPool;
- owner: one theorem per box plus Passes;
- mix-outputs: every output position, value, address, datum and inline case;
- anytx-mix-outputs: two Booleans put the bad output at each of positions 1..n (n = 3, 4);
- box-shapes: its 16 shapes cover every non-box inline datum;
- signers: modules 4..128, with every one of the k signers in the disjunction and k-argument guards;
- slice: 0..255 in four modules of 64, plus two off-byte theorems, matched exhaustively in Rule.

check.sh reads verdicts correctly:
- rc comes from PIPESTATUS[0];
- a `blaster` tactic left Undetermined keeps its goal open, an unsolved-goals error (FAILED);
- a `#blaster` Undetermined is a "⚠️ Undetermined" warning, which Lake prints as `warning: …` (UNDETERM); an expected Undetermined is info, so it raises no false alarm;
- Falsified and Unexpected Valid are errors;
- a timeout (124) and an OOM kill (137) are both reported;
- replayed logs keep their warnings.

